{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '710,758p;777,872p;940,1003p;1022,1115p;1190,1285p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/rule_r_test.cljc | sed -n '420,532p'\"","aggregated_output":"   710\t\n   711\t\n   712\t(defn bounded-row-evaluator\n   713\t  \"The default body runner (§5.2): a fresh throwaway ast-walker loaded from\n   714\t   the lambda body's rows, its parameters bound in `env`, the closed\n   715\t   `prelude` as its only primitives, no store, no module resolver, no stream\n   716\t   constructor, and no FFI bridge. It counts VM transitions.\n   717\t\n   718\t   Returns `{:value v}`, or `{:error e}` with `e` one of\n   719\t   `{:kind :fuel-guard :steps n}`, `{:kind :suspended}` (a park, resume,\n   720\t   bridge call, blocked read, or work scheduled outside the body\n   721\t   continuation), `{:kind :effect-guard :tag t}` (a stream constructor), or\n   722\t   `{:kind :body-error :message s}` (the body threw).\n   723\t\n   724\t   `contract` is the packet's own AST stamp, carried from its store entry\n   725\t   by `invoke`, which has verified it; the body rows load under that stamp,\n   726\t   never one this runner supplies, and a missing or old stamp is refused\n   727\t   (thrown) before anything runs.\"\n   728\t  [{:keys [macro-tree contract env prelude max-steps]}]\n   729\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract contract)\n   730\t  (let [index (packet-index macro-tree)\n   731\t        body (nth (get index (first macro-tree)) 3)\n   732\t        body-set {:root body, :rows (into {} (map (fn [a] [a (get index a)]))\n   733\t                                          (reachable index body))}]\n   734\t    (try\n   735\t      (loop [v (ast-walker/vm-load-rows\n   736\t                 (ast-walker/create-vm {:env env, :primitives prelude,\n   737\t                                        :primitive-profiles {}})\n   738\t                 body-set\n   739\t                 contract)\n   740\t             steps 0]\n   741\t        (let [tag (:type (:control v))]\n   742\t          (cond (or (:blocked? v) (seq (:wait-set v)) (seq (:parked v)))\n   743\t                {:error {:kind :suspended}}\n   744\t\n   745\t                (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? v) {:value (:value v)}\n   746\t\n   747\t                (:halted? v) {:error {:kind :suspended}}\n   748\t\n   749\t                (>= steps max-steps) {:error {:kind :fuel-guard, :steps steps}}\n   750\t\n   751\t                (contains? suspending-tags tag) {:error {:kind :suspended}}\n   752\t\n   753\t                (contains? effect-tags tag) {:error {:kind :effect-guard, :tag tag}}\n   754\t\n   755\t                :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc steps)))))\n   756\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   757\t        {:error {:kind :body-error, :message (catch-message e)}}))))\n   758\t\n   777\t\n   778\t(defn- attempt-id\n   779\t  [ctx counter]\n   780\t  [(get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token]) counter])\n   781\t\n   782\t\n   783\t(defn macro-entry\n   784\t  \"A macro-store value: a self-contained lambda tree `packet` with the AST\n   785\t   `contract` it was produced under. The store holds only these. The\n   786\t   transformer runner verifies the contract before it executes the packet\n   787\t   (Rule R: a persistent or supplied code packet is never relabelled), and\n   788\t   the expander stamps only what it harvests itself, under\n   789\t   `vm/ast-contract`.\"\n   790\t  [packet contract]\n   791\t  {:yin.macro/tree packet, :yin.macro/contract contract})\n   792\t\n   793\t\n   794\t(defn- verified-tree\n   795\t  \"The packet of a macro-store value after its contract is verified\n   796\t   against `vm/ast-contract`: `:contract-missing` for a bare packet or an\n   797\t   entry without one, `:contract-mismatch` for an old stamp.\"\n   798\t  [entry]\n   799\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract\n   800\t                      (when (map? entry) (:yin.macro/contract entry)))\n   801\t  (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n   802\t\n   803\t\n   804\t(defn- check-store!\n   805\t  \"A supplied macro store: no reserved name is a macro (Rule R), and every\n   806\t   entry carries the current AST contract. Returns `store`.\"\n   807\t  [store]\n   808\t  (vm/check-bindings! :macro store)\n   809\t  (doseq [entry (vals store)] (verified-tree entry))\n   810\t  store)\n   811\t\n   812\t\n   813\t(defn- invoke*\n   814\t  \"Run one macro body. `entry` is a macro-store value (`macro-entry`),\n   815\t   verified before anything runs. `counter` is the attempt counter, which\n   816\t   gensyms read. `{:tree packet}` or `{:error e}`.\"\n   817\t  [entry operands ctx counter]\n   818\t  (let [macro-tree (verified-tree entry)\n   819\t        macro-root (first macro-tree)\n   820\t        params (nth (root-row macro-tree) 2)\n   821\t        {:keys [env expected got]} (bind-arguments params operands)]\n   822\t    (if-not env\n   823\t      {:error {:kind :arity, :macro macro-root, :expected expected, :got got}}\n   824\t      (let [n (volatile! 0)\n   825\t            token (get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token])\n   826\t            gensym (fn [prefix]\n   827\t                     (let [i @n]\n   828\t                       (vswap! n inc)\n   829\t                       (symbol (str (if (symbol? prefix) (name prefix) prefix)\n   830\t                                    \"__\" token \"_\" counter \"_\" i))))\n   831\t            run (or (:eval ctx) bounded-row-evaluator)\n   832\t            {:keys [value error]} (run {:macro-tree macro-tree,\n   833\t                                        :contract (:yin.macro/contract entry),\n   834\t                                        :env env,\n   835\t                                        :prelude (prelude gensym),\n   836\t                                        :max-steps (get-in ctx [:guards :max-steps])})]\n   837\t        (if error\n   838\t          {:error (assoc error :macro macro-root)}\n   839\t          {:tree value})))))\n   840\t\n   841\t\n   842\t(def default-guards\n   843\t  {:max-depth 100,\n   844\t   :max-rows-per-expansion 10000,\n   845\t   :max-rows-per-batch nil,\n   846\t   :max-steps 100000})\n   847\t\n   848\t\n   849\t(defn invoke\n   850\t  \"Run `entry`, a macro-store value (`macro-entry`: a self-contained lambda\n   851\t   packet and its AST contract), on `operand-trees` and return its result\n   852\t   tree packet, unvalidated. The contract is verified first\n   853\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`, thrown). Gensyms use\n   854\t   `(:attempt ctx)` as the attempt counter. Throws `ex-info` carrying the\n   855\t   error data on an arity, guard, suspension, or body failure.\"\n   856\t  [entry operand-trees ctx]\n   857\t  (let [ctx (update ctx :guards #(merge default-guards %))\n   858\t        {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry (vec operand-trees) ctx\n   859\t                                      (:attempt ctx))]\n   860\t    (when error\n   861\t      (throw (ex-info \"Macro invocation failed\" error)))\n   862\t    tree))\n   863\t\n   864\t\n   865\t;; =============================================================================\n   866\t;; Tail marking and lowering (§6, §3.2 steps 6-7)\n   867\t;; =============================================================================\n   868\t\n   869\t(defn- retail\n   870\t  \"Recompute every `tail?` slot below `root`, in context `tail?`, over a\n   871\t   working index; `[index' root']`. Tail-ness is contextual, so one shared\n   872\t   row in two contexts becomes two rows.\"\n   940\t  \"Initial harvest: iterate definitions in ordinal order; a declared one\n   941\t   installs its lambda packet, a plain one removes the name. Last wins.\n   942\t   A reserved name is never a definition key or a macro name (Rule R).\"\n   943\t  [store index-of definitions]\n   944\t  (reduce (fn [store {:keys [tree name value declared?]}]\n   945\t            (when (vm/reserved-name? name)\n   946\t              (vm/refuse-reserved! :definition-key name))\n   947\t            (if declared?\n   948\t              (assoc store name\n   949\t                     (macro-entry (packet-of (index-of tree) value)\n   950\t                                  vm/ast-contract))\n   951\t              (dissoc store name)))\n   952\t          store\n   953\t          definitions))\n   954\t\n   955\t\n   956\t(defn- post-harvest\n   957\t  \"The next batch's store: start from the store before initial harvest and\n   958\t   walk the final occurrence tree in declaration order — for an application\n   959\t   whose operator is a lambda, operands left to right then the lambda body;\n   960\t   otherwise child slots in grammar order. A plain definition removes its\n   961\t   name; a stand-in whose `k` exists and whose catalogue name matches\n   962\t   installs that entry; later occurrences win.\"\n   963\t  [store index root catalogue]\n   964\t  (letfn [(children\n   965\t            [row]\n   966\t            (let [places (child-places row)]\n   967\t              (if (and (= :application (row-tag row))\n   968\t                       (= :lambda (row-tag (get index (nth row 2)))))\n   969\t                (concat (map second (rest places))\n   970\t                        [(nth (get index (nth row 2)) 3)])\n   971\t                (map second places))))\n   972\t          (walk\n   973\t            [store a]\n   974\t            (let [row (get index a)\n   975\t                  store (cond\n   976\t                          (= standin-tag (row-tag row))\n   977\t                          (let [[_ _ nm k] row\n   978\t                                entry (get catalogue k)]\n   979\t                            (if (and entry (= nm (:name entry)))\n   980\t                              (assoc store nm\n   981\t                                     (macro-entry (:macro-tree entry)\n   982\t                                                  vm/ast-contract))\n   983\t                              store))\n   984\t\n   985\t                          :else\n   986\t                          (if-let [{:keys [name]} (definition-at index a)]\n   987\t                            (dissoc store name)\n   988\t                            store))]\n   989\t              (reduce walk store (children row))))]\n   990\t    (walk store root)))\n   991\t\n   992\t\n   993\t;; =============================================================================\n   994\t;; Events (§8)\n   995\t;; =============================================================================\n   996\t\n   997\t(defn- event-row\n   998\t  [attempt source-batch origin parent input-root call-path macro-root output-root error]\n   999\t  (intern-row [:yin.macro/expand attempt source-batch origin parent input-root\n  1000\t               call-path macro-root output-root error]))\n  1001\t\n  1002\t\n  1003\t(defn- source-origin\n  1022\t\n  1023\t(defn- macro-of\n  1024\t  \"The stored macro packet for an operator occurrence: a `:variable` naming\n  1025\t   a store entry that no enclosing lambda parameter shadows.\"\n  1026\t  [st operator shadow]\n  1027\t  (let [row (get (:index st) operator)]\n  1028\t    (when (and (= :variable (row-tag row))\n  1029\t               (not (contains? shadow (nth row 2))))\n  1030\t      (get (:store st) (nth row 2)))))\n  1031\t\n  1032\t\n  1033\t(defn- record-event\n  1034\t  [st event-row*]\n  1035\t  (update st :events conj event-row*))\n  1036\t\n  1037\t\n  1038\t(defn- guard-batch-rows\n  1039\t  [st]\n  1040\t  (let [limit (get-in st [:ctx :guards :max-rows-per-batch])\n  1041\t        n (count (:index st))]\n  1042\t    (when (and limit (> n limit))\n  1043\t      {:kind :row-guard, :scope :batch, :rows n})))\n  1044\t\n  1045\t\n  1046\t(defn- merge-output\n  1047\t  \"Merge a validated result packet into the working index; an address whose\n  1048\t   working body differs is an `:address-conflict`.\"\n  1049\t  [st [_ rows]]\n  1050\t  (reduce (fn [st row]\n  1051\t            (let [prior (get (:index st) (first row))]\n  1052\t              (cond (nil? prior) (assoc-in st [:index (first row)] row)\n  1053\t                    (same-value? prior row) st\n  1054\t                    :else (reduced (assoc st ::conflict (first row))))))\n  1055\t          st\n  1056\t          rows))\n  1057\t\n  1058\t\n  1059\t(declare expand-node)\n  1060\t\n  1061\t\n  1062\t(defn- expand-call\n  1063\t  \"One recognized call: allocate an attempt, begin its event before any\n  1064\t   guard or invocation, run the transformer on the operand packets, validate\n  1065\t   and merge the result, finish the event, and reconsider the result at the\n  1066\t   same occurrence with depth + 1.\"\n  1067\t  [st address entry {:keys [path rel frame shadow depth]}]\n  1068\t  (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt st)\n  1069\t        ctx (:ctx st)\n  1070\t        macro-root (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n  1071\t        begin (fn [output error]\n  1072\t                (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter)\n  1073\t                           (:source-batch st)\n  1074\t                           (when-not (:parent frame)\n  1075\t                             (source-origin ctx (:source-batch st) (:tree-index frame)))\n  1076\t                           (:parent frame)\n  1077\t                           (:root frame)\n  1078\t                           rel\n  1079\t                           macro-root\n  1080\t                           output\n  1081\t                           error))\n  1082\t        failed (fn [st error]\n  1083\t                 (-> st (record-event (begin nil error)) (fail error)))\n  1084\t        guards (:guards ctx)]\n  1085\t    (if (>= depth (:max-depth guards))\n  1086\t      [(failed st {:kind :depth-guard, :depth depth, :path path}) address]\n  1087\t      (let [row (get (:index st) address)\n  1088\t            operands (mapv #(packet-of (:index st) %) (nth row 3))\n  1089\t            {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry operands ctx counter)\n  1090\t            invalid (fn [reason]\n  1091\t                      {:kind :invalid-output, :macro macro-root, :path path,\n  1092\t                       :reason reason})]\n  1093\t        (if error\n  1094\t          [(failed st error) address]\n  1095\t          (if-let [e (valid-tree? tree {:working? true})]\n  1096\t            [(failed st (invalid (:reason e))) address]\n  1097\t            (let [n (count (set (map first (second tree))))]\n  1098\t              (if (> n (:max-rows-per-expansion guards))\n  1099\t                [(failed st {:kind :row-guard, :scope :expansion, :rows n}) address]\n  1100\t                (let [st' (merge-output st tree)]\n  1101\t                  (if (::conflict st')\n  1102\t                    [(failed st (invalid :address-conflict)) address]\n  1103\t                    (if-let [e (guard-batch-rows st')]\n  1104\t                      [(failed st' e) address]\n  1105\t                      (let [out (first tree)\n  1106\t                            ev (begin out nil)\n  1107\t                            st' (-> st'\n  1108\t                                    (record-event ev)\n  1109\t                                    (update :produced\n  1110\t                                            (fn [p]\n  1111\t                                              (if (some #(= out (first %)) p)\n  1112\t                                                p\n  1113\t                                                (conj p (packet-of (:index st') out))))))]\n  1114\t                        (expand-node st' out\n  1115\t                                     {:path path,\n  1190\t\n  1191\t(defn- with-default-guards\n  1192\t  [ctx]\n  1193\t  (update ctx :guards #(merge default-guards %)))\n  1194\t\n  1195\t\n  1196\t(defn expand-batch\n  1197\t  \"Expand one input batch against `ctx` (§3.2). Returns\n  1198\t   `{:status :ok :tree packet :log log :ctx ctx'}` or\n  1199\t   `{:status :error :error e :log log :ctx ctx'}`. Either way `ctx'` has\n  1200\t   consumed the batch (`:t` + 1) and every attempt it allocated; only\n  1201\t   success changes the store, to the post-harvest store. A context store\n  1202\t   binding a reserved name, or holding an entry without the current AST\n  1203\t   contract, is refused (Rule R): it is a composition defect, so it throws\n  1204\t   rather than returning an error.\"\n  1205\t  [batch ctx]\n  1206\t  (check-store! (:store ctx))\n  1207\t  (let [ctx (with-default-guards ctx)\n  1208\t        source-batch (:t ctx)\n  1209\t        base {:ctx ctx, :source-batch source-batch, :events [], :produced []}\n  1210\t        finish (fn [st]\n  1211\t                 (let [ctx' (update (:ctx st) :t inc)]\n  1212\t                   (if-let [e (:error st)]\n  1213\t                     {:status :error, :error e, :log (log-packet st), :ctx ctx'}\n  1214\t                     {:status :ok, :tree (:tree st), :log (log-packet st),\n  1215\t                      :ctx (assoc ctx' :store (:next-store st))})))\n  1216\t        {:keys [admitted error]} (admit batch)]\n  1217\t    (if error\n  1218\t      (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt base)]\n  1219\t        (finish (-> st\n  1220\t                    (record-event (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter) source-batch\n  1221\t                                             (source-origin ctx source-batch nil)\n  1222\t                                             nil nil nil nil nil error))\n  1223\t                    (fail error))))\n  1224\t      (let [{:keys [trees indexes index run-index definitions]} admitted\n  1225\t            store0 (or (:store ctx) {})\n  1226\t            store (harvest store0 #(nth indexes %) definitions)\n  1227\t            catalogue (into []\n  1228\t                            (comp (filter :declared?)\n  1229\t                                  (map (fn [{:k