                               \".\"\n    77\t                                           (clojure.core/name name)))))]\n    78\t          resolved\n    79\t          (fail (str \"Unable to resolve symbol: \" name \" in this context\")\n    80\t                {:symbol name}))))))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn check-store-key!\n    84\t  \"Refuse a program store access whose key is a reserved name (Rule R):\n    85\t   the definition operator is never a store key.\"\n    86\t  [key]\n    87\t  (when (vm/reserved-name? key)\n    88\t    (vm/refuse-reserved! :store-key key)))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn store-put\n    92\t  \"The one program store write: every definition transition, the\n    93\t   `:vm/store-put` effect, and the four direct store instructions write\n    94\t   through here, and a reserved key is refused. Every other store write\n    95\t   `yin.vm.store-write-audit-test` detects is state construction on its\n    96\t   allowlist; that namespace states what it detects and the residual it\n    97\t   leaves to review.\"\n    98\t  [store key val]\n    99\t  (check-store-key! key)\n   100\t  (assoc store key val))\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn- gen-id\n   104\t  \"Generate a unique keyword ID from a prefix and counter value.\"\n   105\t  [prefix id-counter]\n   106\t  (keyword (str prefix \"-\" id-counter)))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(defn vm-blocked?\n   110\t  \"Returns true if the VM is blocked.\"\n   111\t  [vm]\n   112\t  (boolean (:blocked? vm)))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn vm-value\n   505\t(defn gensym\n   506\t  \"Generate a unique ID and return [id updated-state].\"\n   507\t  ([state] (gensym state \"id\"))\n   508\t  ([state prefix]\n   509\t   (let [id-counter (or (:id-counter state) 0)\n   510\t         id (gen-id prefix id-counter)]\n   511\t     [id (assoc state :id-counter (inc id-counter))])))\n   512\t\n   513\t\n   514\t(defn handle-stream-block\n   515\t  [result entry]\n   516\t  (if (:park result)\n   517